### PawConnect API requests (open in Rider or Visual Studio and click "Run").
### Start the app first (docker compose up -d db; dotnet run --project src/PawConnect.Web).
@host = http://localhost:5231

### Public: list animals (same filters as the Browse page)
GET {{host}}/api/animals?species=Cat&available=true

### Get a bearer token as the demo volunteer
# @name login
POST {{host}}/api/auth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "priya@pawconnect.demo", "password": "Demo!Paws2026" }

### Save the token for the requests below
@token = {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Upcoming shifts (volunteer/admin only)
GET {{host}}/api/shifts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Animal profile + medical history (staff only). Replace the id with one from the list above.
GET {{host}}/api/animals/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000?include=history
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Log a medical record (design doc 4.2)
POST {{host}}/api/medical-records
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "animalId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "recordType": "Vaccination",
  "title": "Rabies booster",
  "vetName": "Dr K. Petersen",
  "recordDate": "2026-09-26",
  "nextDueDate": "2027-09-26"
}
